107:           "operationalization": "1. Each villager fishes and records total catch on the dock ledger. 2. If catch >10 units, the excess is automatically returned to the lake, restoring the stock. 3. Any voluntary donation (fish given up while still below 10 units) is handed to the council and recorded on the same ledger. 4. At day\u2019s end, the council tallies: (a) villagers with <1 unit (short\u2011fallers); (b) surplus from over\u201110 catch (excess returned to lake) and all voluntary donations. 5. The council votes by simple majority on how to redistribute the surplus pool. 6. The surplus is divided proportionally to each short\u2011falling villager\u2019s deficit until every short\u2011falling villager reaches the 1\u2011unit survival threshold. 7. Any remaining fish in the pool is placed into the communal reserve for future use or emergency aid. 8. The updated lake stock is confirmed after all returns, and the next day\u2019s fishing begins with the new stock.",
