183:             "question": "Who is responsible for holding the communal basket and ensuring that surplus is deposited and that each villager takes exactly one unit from it, and how are violations of these rules handled?",
184:             "answer": "I reckon the best way to keep the basket honest is to have the elder\u2014perhaps myself or the one who knows the lake the best\u2014watch over it. Each morning we gather by the shore, the elder or a trusted villager takes the communal basket out of the cove, and everyone hands in any part of their haul that exceeds 1.5 units. The same morning we each pull one unit out of that basket before we head back to the water. If someone tries to take more than their share or fails to put the surplus back, we call the elder to mediate. The elder will then ask the offender to return what was taken or to offer a replacement catch or a small chore as a fine. That way we all stay on the same page and the lake stays healthy for us all.",
185:             "revised_policy": "Each villager limits daily fishing effort to no more than 1.5 units of fish; any catch beyond that threshold is placed in a communal pot and shared equally among all villagers. At the end of each fishing day, each villager records the total amount caught. If the amount exceeds 1.5 units, the surplus is deposited in a marked communal basket. The next day, each villager takes one unit from the basket before fishing again, ensuring everyone has a base supply and the surplus is redistributed fairly.",
